                "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 25 at 10:30AM AKST until November 28 at 6:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Coastal Flooding with water levels 1.5 to 3.0 feet above\nthe highest tide line possible.\n\n* WHERE...Kipnuk and Kwigillingok\n\n* WHEN...6 PM Thursday to 6 AM Saturday. Particularly the\novernight tide cycles Thursday night and Friday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Potential flooding of low lying areas, including\nlowest portions of boardwalks. Coastal erosion possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A long duration of southerly winds combined\nwith the high tide cycle will increase the potential for\nelevated water levels, high surf, and coastal erosion Thursday\nnight and Friday night. For Saturday Night, though winds will be\nweaker and oriented more offshore, the tide cycle will remain\nhigh. Water levels are expected to be lower compared to Thursday\nNight and Friday, however there still is some potential for\ncoastal erosion. Stay tuned for forecast updates.",
                "instruction": "A coastal flood advisory indicates that onshore winds and tides\nwill combine to generate flooding of low areas along the shore.",
                "response": "Monitor",
                "note": null,
